  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: 'to' before Gezer moved from the infinitive bo' to the place name. Gezer is an adverbial accusative of direction, not the verb's direct object, so rule 33 governs the supplied preposition and rule 44's supplied-object clause does not reach it; this matches the chapter's treatment of 'to Jerusalem' at 2SA.5.6."
